    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Doublespeak is the self-titled debut album by Doublespeak, the collaboration between Erasure’s Vince Clarke, Blancmange’s Neil Arthur, and electronic producer-writer Benge. Released on London Records, it presents eleven songs spanning four decades as a synth-driven reimagining of material drawn from post-punk, art-pop, and mainstream pop sources.\n\nThe album’s range is part of its appeal: it moves from darker, more angular songs by artists such as Fad Gadget, The Sound, and Young Marble Giants to glossy pop touchstones associated with ABBA, David Essex, and The Carpenters, while also reaching into later material by The Magnetic Fields, Ed Dowie, and Laptop. Reviewers highlighted the balance of affection and invention in the performances, noting that the record works as a covers album by transforming familiar songs through analogue electronics, bold arrangements, and empathic vocals.",
